From b5fdca891b648790ad323e50be3fc9a2670fe9e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:10:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop inventing bus times: make journey search direction-aware

Searching A -> B and B -> A returned the same buses at the same times for
394 routes. Routes without a timetable, and the middle stops of routes that
have one, got departures generated from a fixed 06:00, 06:25, ... pattern
with a 45 minute trip, ignoring the route and the direction.

- Remove estimatedTrips. The site never shows a time it cannot back up.
- Middle-stop searches on timetabled routes derive times from that run's real
  terminal times, using outbound times one way and return times the other,
  and mark them approximate (~) in the cards, modal and transfer plans.
- Routes with no published times are listed as "connects your stops, no
  timetable yet" (findRouteLinks + RouteLinks) with no times at all.
- Changes between approximate buses need a 10 minute margin instead of 4.
- Drop saved "recently viewed" entries whose trip ids no longer exist.
- Point the Parnashree search alias at the real stop (Parnasree Pally).
- Add npm test: 17 regression tests over every route and every pair of its
  stops in both directions, including the reported Howrah Railway Station
  <-> Salt Lake Sector V journey. Verified to fail if the old behaviour
  returns.
- Document the departure kinds in the README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018DmTGSb3B3m714Z76vmAQT
